       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the typical 1,000 mg maximum. At this dose, the risk of serious hepatotoxicity is high, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day), a conservative standard regimen.\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day), the maximum standard daily dose.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n\nIf 2,000 mg was a typo, for example if you meant 1,000 mg or 2,000 mg/day total, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. I'd still recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
